  hetu: the defect is in MY LOOKING, not in the object.  dosa 0002 recorded its replay as a LINE RANGE, `sed -n '2400,2410p' machine/MathMachine.hs`, and a concurrent agent added 125 lines to that file between the write and the replay.  The command now prints a passage about Tusnim and residual triage.  A line number is not a name for a piece of code; it is a name for a position, and positions move
  hetu: so no verdict on the object may be read out of that replay.  The DIVERGED it printed does not mean the defect was repaired.  Kumarila's condition is not met: the looking would not have apprehended the thing had it been there, because the looking was pointed at coordinates rather than at content
  nasta: what a bare "DIVERGED" would have destroyed, had it been read as a repair: the defect is still exactly present, at machine/MathMachine.hs:2522-2523 -- `case code of / ExitSuccess -> do / hPrintf logh "  KERNEL-ACCEPT round=%d %s = %s"` -- unchanged in content and moved by 120 lines
  nasta: and dosa 0001's naṣṭa is likewise still present, now at machine/MathMachine.hs:2527-2530: `ExitFailure _ -> do / hPrintf ... (take 160 (filter (/= '\n') (out ++ err))) / pure False`
  nasta: the stale coordinates themselves, which cannot be struck: dosa 0001 vastu says :2408 and dosa 0002 vastu says :2402-2406.  Both were true when written.  Read today they point into the middle of somebody else's insertion
